# Briefing: Harden the parser against <script> tags & "quoted" input

**Stack:** Rust 1.98, serde & serde_yaml

## Constraints

### Hard (Non-negotiable)

<rules priority="required">
- When working in `src/**/*.rs`: MUST: Reject input containing `<` or `&` unless it is escaped
- Keep `Record<T>` generics intact in error messages
</rules>

### Soft (Preferred)

<rules priority="preferred">
- PREFER: `&str` over `String` in the "hot" paths
</rules>

### Ask First (Requires approval)

<rules priority="ask-first">
- STOP and confirm with the user before: Changing the <envelope> tag vocabulary
</rules>

## Sacred Regions (Do Not Modify)

The following files and directories must not be modified under any circumstances. If a task requires changes to these paths, STOP and report the conflict.

<protected_files>
- `src/**/*.rs` — Every Rust source file, including "generated" ones
- `docs/a&b/**` — Ampersand in a path
</protected_files>

## Reference Context

Read these files for background before starting work:

<context>
- @docs/a<b>.md
</context>

## Identity

The `<brief>` envelope team — owners of A & B.

## Assumptions

<assumptions>
- [ ] Input can carry a fenced code block with markup
- [x] Both `'` and `"` survive the round-trip
</assumptions>

## Deliverable

<deliverable>
Well-formed XML whose text keeps A & B < C > D and 'single' and "double" quotes intact.
</deliverable>

## Notes

A fenced block with markup in it:

```rust
fn main() {
    if a < b && c > d {
        println!("{}", "<tag attr='v'>");
    }
}
```
